{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>I will be</b> — The opposite of their root. \"Yaveish\" and \"yevosh\" are its root (meaning \"to be dry\"). And the rose shall blossom speedily. And because it has no root but a thin one, he said, \"and his roots shall be like the root of the trees of Lebanon.\"" "<b>And his roots shall strike</b> — In length and in breadth, like \"and wipe toward the shoulder of the sea of Kinneret,\" and in the measurements of fractions and Tabritha."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:15.986463860Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}